[Music]  my name is eddie mexion co-founder and  owner of known as empanadas we're  located in beverly hills and west  hollywood in los angeles california well  known as empanadas is a combination of  several things in the front we have a  beautiful quick service restaurant but  we bake and serve over 30 flavors of  empanadas any given time and in the back  is a full production kitchen we have  many types of flavors with meat  vegetable cheese even dessert whatever  you're craving known as has an empanada  for you empanada comes from the spanish  verb empanada which means to cover in  dough or pastry so an empanada is  essentially any filling covered in dough  some of our most popular empanadas have  always been the beef and veggie our  signature beef filling starts by  sauteing onions then we add ground beef  once the beef is cooked we remove the  fat  add butter and mix it in we then add our  blend of spices which is made up of salt  black pepper oregano paprika and red  peppers once everything is mixed we let  it rest for a few minutes spread it on a  sheet pan you send it to the blast  chiller to cool down  once the filling is cool we mix in green  onions green olives hard boiled eggs we  then mix everything together again and  that's how we make our signature beef  filling  to make our classic veggie filling we  start by cooking spinach diced carrots  and broccoli while those are cooling we  saute garlic and onions with a blend of  spices and send that to chill  once our veggies are cooled we chop up  the spinach the broccoli we mix it in  with the garlic and onions and the diced  carrots and we mix in green peas  corn red peppers feta and parmesan  cheese we then mix all the ingredients  together by hand and that's our classic  veggie filling  and finally it's time to make the  empanadas when we first started we made  the empanadas by hand by folding the  edge we had different folding techniques  depending on the flavor of empanada that  was the original way to distinguish what  you were eating as the business grew it  was difficult to keep up with demand so  we then moved to using custom hand  operated empanada molds to close the  empanadas but even the hand press wasn't  efficient enough in the past year we've  averaged 15 to 20 000 empanadas a week  so we imported a custom empanada folding  machine from argentina  [Music]  it takes three people to operate the  machine one person places the dough into  the mold another person puts the filling  into the mold the machine then closes  the empanada and then feeds the finished  empanada to the end of the line where  the third person puts it on a tray each  tray holds about 40 empanadas when the  machine is operating at full speed it  can make 1 700 empanadas an hour once  the tray is complete we send it off to  cool and store overnight so they're  ready to bake serve and enjoy the next  day  every empanada is branded with our logo  and flavor so you know what you're about  to enjoy when you come to nona's you're  hit by this wonderful smell of freshly  baked empanadas you then see this  beautiful bright display case full of  empanadas with more flavors than you can  imagine there is no one perfect empanada  but what makes the empanada perfect is  the unlimited flavor combinations it's  portable it's handy you can enjoy it  anywhere anytime it really is the  perfect finger food  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you

